    "Patterns operate on Unicode scalar values, not visible grapheme clusters. \\d means ASCII digits; \\w uses the specified Unicode alphabetic, mark, decimal-number and connector-punctuation categories. Spans and compile-error positions use UTF-8 bytes. No implicit String-to-Regex conversion occurs, and the runtime does not delegate semantics to the host JavaScript engine."
